the nba playoffs resumed today following  a three-day players-led boycott of games  the pause as they've called it came in  the wake of jacob blake's shooting  they are returning to the court after  agreeing with nba owners on a unified  action plan to fight racial injustice  which includes working to turn arenas  and possibly practice facilities into  voting locations for the upcoming  election  during that pause i spoke with nba  players association vice president andre  iguodala  who shared some of the players mindset  from the nba bubble in orlando  can you give us a sense of what it is  like for you with so much going on  outside that you want to be a part of  but knowing that you have a platform by  playing inside that bubble  yeah it's one of those circumstances  where it can be the perfect storm  uh for the mind to kind of you know tear  you down but i think what we've been  able to do is  knowing before we got here you know  we're coming here with a purpose  understanding it so we realized it was  the ultimate decision was to come down  here and play  for something bigger than ourselves and  bigger than basketball and  a lot of people don't want to talk about  the financial aspect of it but you know  building  building wealth for our communities uh  you know  us being able to accumulate that wealth  and then being able to take it back to  our communities  and at the same time bringing the  awareness which is the main goal coming  out here  shedding the light using this platform  you know you're seeing a lot of  reactions to what we've been doing from  other leagues and and that shows a lot  of power  or a lot of influence that we're having  and using the influence in the right way  just to shed light  on a lot of the social injustices that  have been occurring it's just the  beginning of time  i think doc rivers said that you love  this country but the country  isn't loving you back and i i had an  interesting uh  conversation with killer mike uh who's a  rapper and we've had many great  conversations before coming to the  bubble  things we should try to do to bring more  awareness to the situation and then try  to build up our communities  through our platform as well and he had  similar uh sentiments and saying you  know  it's interesting how we've been all over  the world but  you know at the end of the day we still  would rather live here  and that's the struggle in the mind  constantly  you know just looking for a place in the  world where we're accepted as equals  what did it come down to for all of you  to agree that you wanted to keep playing  i think ultimately it's it's you know we  wanted to  take a step back we wanted to regroup  refocus and just like a refresh button  because it's just  things can get heavy in your heart and  you know sometimes you ask yourself  what's your purpose  and what it boils down to is is the  platform working for us to  get our messages out there and there's a  real human issue here  and we're just trying to shed light on  that and we're going to try to  put things in place to change that so it  was really the platform  understanding how big our platform is  and when they've been telling us to shut  up  and and dribble because they don't want  to hear his talk so we realize if we  aren't playing  it's going to shut us up and we're not  going to be dribbling so you kind of get  hit  with the double whammy and we realize  you know we can we can have just as much  leverage doing both you know playing and  speaking and  being about change and the action is  there anything else that you would want  people to know about what's been going  on  there in orlando over the last couple  days that maybe we're misunderstanding  or not seeing  uh you know i think you look at the  athlete and it goes all the way back to  you know uh you know greek mythology and  we looked at these godlike beings but at  the end of the day we're humans  and you know we have feelings we have  emotions and although we get people  away from their issues and bring joy to  them we need time to  focus on our mental health as well and a  big part of that is  uh you know you want the next generation  to be better than you are  and and wouldn't be right if we left  those uh  communities that we grew up in we left  them behind when situations like this  happen  and that's why i wear group economics on  the back of my jerseys it's all about  building up my community and trying to  close that wealth gap  and again if you just look at it they  were so worried that their voices were  not being heard because they were there  people were focusing on the play  this was their moment to say hey pay  attention and now they're taking action  so you look at those action steps like  trying to help with voter registration  and combat some of these injustices  interesting to hear about what might  happen in some of these the arenas of  the stadium  both before the election and after right  and now that's their push yeah when they  stopped playing  they got our attention
 

